  {"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"When does Wynn Al Marjan Island open?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Wynn Al Marjan Island is scheduled to open in 2027. Almost every current launch on the island is priced against that date."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How many off-plan launches are there on Al Marjan Island, and at what prices?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Our current book carries 9 launches on Al Marjan Island, with developer entry prices from AED 920,000 to AED 4.06M."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What payment plans are typical on Al Marjan Island launches?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Plans typically run from 50/50 to 80/20, paid in stages as the building is constructed."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What do furnished one-bedrooms rent for on Al Marjan Island?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Furnished one-bedrooms in our book sit between AED 65,000 and AED 90,000 a year; two-bedroom duplexes rent for more."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is Ras Al Khaimah a good place to buy property?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Often, yes: freehold ownership for foreigners, no property tax, a Golden Visa route from AED 2M, and limited beachfront supply. Growth has been slower than Dubai and new supply is arriving, so it suits buyers who check the details rather than following the story alone."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does buying property in Ras Al Khaimah give you a Golden Visa?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"It can. Property worth AED 2M or more can qualify you for a UAE Golden Visa, subject to the federal ICP rules at the time you apply. Official pages differ on whether the property route gives 5 or 10 years: ICP and RAKEZ describe 10 years, while the u.ae portal lists 5 years for real estate investments. RFR does not issue visas or give immigration advice."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What are the risks of buying property in Ras Al Khaimah?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Slower price growth than earlier in 2026, a large supply pipeline (more than 34,000 units expected between 2026 and 2030, per CBRE), handover dates that can slip, service charges that vary by building, and rental demand around the new resort that is not yet known. Confirm the freehold status of the exact unit and the current rules with the authority before you pay a deposit."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is Ras Al Khaimah property a good investment in 2026?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Nobody can promise a return. CBRE reported Al Marjan Island apartment values up 23.1% year on year in H1 2026, and ValuStrat put the overall Ras Al Khaimah index up 5.4% on the year in Q2 2026, but both sources show growth slowing during 2026. Past price changes are not a forecast. Check the developer, payment plan, handover date, service charge and evidence of rental demand for the specific unit."}}]}
